169	/****************************************************************************
170	 * Name: exec_spawn
171	 *
172	 * Description:
173	 *   exec() configurable version, delivery the spawn attribute if this
174	 *   process has special customization.
175	 *
176	 * Input Parameters:
177	 *   filename - The path to the program to be executed. If
178	 *              CONFIG_LIBC_ENVPATH is defined in the configuration, then
179	 *              this may be a relative path from the current working
180	 *              directory. Otherwise, path must be the absolute path to the
181	 *              program.
182	 *   argv     - A pointer to an array of string arguments. The end of the
183	 *              array is indicated with a NULL entry.
184	 *   envp     - A pointer to an array of environment strings. Terminated with
185	 *              a NULL entry.
186	 *   exports  - The address of the start of the caller-provided symbol
187	 *              table. This symbol table contains the addresses of symbols
188	 *              exported by the caller and made available for linking the
189	 *              module into the system.
190	 *   nexports - The number of symbols in the exports table.
191	 *   actions  - The spawn file actions
192	 *   attr     - The spawn attributes.
193	 *
194	 * Returned Value:
195	 *   It returns the PID of the exec'ed module.  On failure, it returns
196	 *   the negative errno value appropriately.
197	 *
198	 ****************************************************************************/
